This README file contains information on building the meta-baldeagle
BSP layer, and booting the images contained in the build/tmp/deploy/images/
directory. Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Dependencies
============

This layer depends on:

  URI: git://git.openembedded.org/bitbake
  branch: master

  URI: git://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core
  layers: meta
  branch: master

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Building the meta-baldeagle BSP layer
     > Build dependencies
     > Pre-build steps
     > Building the image

  II. Booting the images in build/tmp/deploy/images/


I. Building the meta-baldeagle BSP layer
--------------------------------------------

Build Dependencies
------------------
        - The base distribution for building Yoctoproject BSP is Ubuntu12.10
		  64-bit.
		
	- The following packages are required to be installed for building
          the yoctoproject BSP image.

          	$ sudo apt-get install gawk wget git-core diffstat unzip \
		  texinfo build-essential chrpath libsdl1.2-dev xterm


Pre-build steps
---------------
        - Extract the AMD BaldEagle BSP package to a directory of choice,
          say /home/amdbaldeagle
                $ tar xjf AMD_Bald_Eagle_yoctoproject_BSP_v1_0_0.tar.bz2

        - Change working directory to
		  AMD_BaldEagle_yoctoproject_BSP_v1_0_0/sources

                $ cd AMD_Bald_Eagle_yoctoproject_BSP_v1_0_0/sources/

        - Extract yoctoproject tarball in the current working directory

                $ tar xjf poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle.tar.bz2

        - Change working directory to 'poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle'
		  directory

                $ cd poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle
        - Set the build environment

                $ source oe-init-build-env

          The above step will set environment variables required to build
          yoctoproject BSP image.

        - Add the baldeagle BSP layer to bblayers.conf file. Eg.

                $ cat conf/bblayers.conf

                # LAYER_CONF_VERSION is increased each time
				build/conf/bblayers.conf
                # changes incompatibly
                LCONF_VERSION = "6"

                BBPATH = "${TOPDIR}"
                BBFILES ?= ""

                BBLAYERS ?= " \

		  /home/amdbaldeagle/poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle/meta \
                  /home/amdbaldeagle/poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle/meta-yocto \
                  /home/amdbaldeagle/poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle/meta-yocto-bsp \
                  /home/amdbaldeagle/poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle/meta-amd/meta-baldeagle \
                  "
                BBLAYERS_NON_REMOVABLE ?= " \
                  /home/amdbaldeagle/poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle/meta \
                  /home/amdbaldeagle/poky-dora-10.0.0_baldeagle/meta-yocto \
                  "

        - Edit the file conf/local.conf file and change the MACHINE variable
          and PACKAGE_CLASSES variable as shown below.

                MACHINE ??= "baldeagle"
                PACKAGE_CLASSES ?= "package_deb"


Building the image 
------------------
        - Run the below command from within 'build' directory

                $ bitbake core-image-sato

        - Once the build succeeds, the image will be placed into the below
          directory

                build/tmp/deploy/images/


II. Booting the images in build/tmp/deploy/images/
--------------------------------------------------

     To write an image into a USB device that will be bootable in
     USB-ZIP mode, carry out the following actions:

     a. Determine the geometry of your USB device using fdisk:

     # fdisk /dev/sdb
     Command (m for help): p

     Disk /dev/sdb: 4011 MB, 4011491328 bytes
     124 heads, 62 sectors/track, 1019 cylinders, total 7834944 sectors
     ...

     Command (m for help): q

     b. Configure the USB device for USB-ZIP mode:

     # mkdiskimage -4 /dev/sdb 1019 124 62

     Where 1019, 124 and 62 are the cylinder, head and sectors/track counts
     as reported by fdisk (substitute the values reported for your device).
     When the operation has finished and the access LED (if any) on the
     device stops flashing, remove and reinsert the device to allow the
     kernel to detect the new partition layout.

     c. Copy the contents of the image to the USB-ZIP mode device:

     # mkdir /tmp/image
     # mkdir /tmp/usbkey
     # mount -o loop core-image-sato-baldeagle.hddimg /tmp/image
     # mount /dev/sdb4 /tmp/usbkey
     # cp -rf /tmp/image/* /tmp/usbkey

     d. Install the syslinux boot loader:

     # syslinux /dev/sdb4

     e. Unmount everything:

     # umount /tmp/image
     # umount /tmp/usbkey

  Install the boot device in the target board and configure the BIOS to boot.
